    {
        "content": "<p>I'm a bit confused about this error I'm getting with the new resolver in 1.14 in a project with both <a href=\"https://juliaregistries.github.io/General/packages/redirect_to_repo/CUDA\">CUDA.jl</a> and <a href=\"https://juliaregistries.github.io/General/packages/redirect_to_repo/DifferentialEquations\">DifferentialEquations.jl</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia console\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"go\">pkg&gt; add CUDA@6.5.1</span>\n<span class=\"go\">   Resolving package versions...</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">ERROR: Unsatisfiable requirements detected — 1 conflict:</span>\n\n<span class=\"gr\">Conflict 1: CUDA and DifferentialEquations</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">  • DifferentialEquations constrains CUDA to ≤6.5.0 (through CUDACore,</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">    OrdinaryDiffEq, Reexport, KernelAbstractions, LinearSolve, NonlinearSolve</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">    and OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock)</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">  • your compat restricts CUDA to 6.5.1</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">  Fix it by any one of:</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">    1. relax your compat on CUDA</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">       → allows: CUDA 6.4.2, DifferentialEquations 8.1.1</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">    2. drop dependency CUDA</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">       → allows: DifferentialEquations 8.1.1</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">  Note: dropping dependency DifferentialEquations would not help unless you</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">    also dropped dependency OrdinaryDiffEq.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In this project the only compat lines I have are:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">[compat]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">CUDA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"6\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Revise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"3\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And I went through the packages listed in the conflict error message, but unless I'm missing something none of them declare any compat with CUDA at all <span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span> Sooo I'm a bit confused. Does anyone know how to find the offending package?</p>\n<p>This is the output of <code>st --outdated</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia console\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"go\">pkg&gt; st --outdated</span>\n<span class=\"go\">Status `/path/to/Project.toml`</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌃ [052768ef] CUDA v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1)</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [bd0ed864] CUDACore v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA, CUDATools, CUPTI, NVML, cuBLAS, cuFFT, cuRAND, cuSOLVER, cuSPARSE</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [9ec180c6] CUDATools v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [63c18a36] KernelAbstractions v0.9.47 (&lt;v0.10.7): CUDACore, cuSPARSE</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌃ [b20c7882] LinearInterpolations v0.1.4 (&lt;v0.1.6)</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [bac558e1] OrderedCollections v1.8.2 (&lt;v2.0.3): DataFramesMeta, PProf, Parameters</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [182d3088] cuBLAS v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA, cuSOLVER</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [533571aa] cuFFT v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [20fd9a0b] cuRAND v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [887afef0] cuSOLVER v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA</span>\n<span class=\"go\">⌅ [b26da814] cuSPARSE v6.4.2 (&lt;v6.5.1): CUDA, cuSOLVER</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 640710322,
        "sender_full_name": "James Wrigley",
        "timestamp": 1794827845
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For example LinearSolve has a weak dependency on CUDA, although not restricted in the way indicated here.</p>\n<p>I think the real problem is that CUDACore 6.5.1 has KernelAbstractions compat of 0.10 but some other of your indirect dependencies holds it back to 0.9.</p>",
        "id": 640735628,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794834355
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Then there's also something that's not completely right with the error messages:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">jl_Adq52L</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pkg</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"err\">@</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.7</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">Resolving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">package</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">versions</span><span class=\"o\">...</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ERROR</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unsatisfiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requirements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">detected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">—</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">conflict</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Conflict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requires</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSolve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">2.30.2</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSolve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">2.30.2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">constrains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≤</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.6</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">your</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">compat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">restricts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.7</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">jl_Adq52L</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pkg</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"err\">@</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.6</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">Resolving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">package</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">versions</span><span class=\"o\">...</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ERROR</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unsatisfiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requirements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">detected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">—</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">conflict</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Conflict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requires</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSolve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">2.30.2</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSolve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">2.30.2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">constrains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≤</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.7</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">your</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">compat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">restricts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.6</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">jl_Adq52L</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pkg</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"err\">@</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.5</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">Resolving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">package</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">versions</span><span class=\"o\">...</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ERROR</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unsatisfiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requirements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">detected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">—</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">conflict</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Conflict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrdinaryDiffEqRosenbrock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requires</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSolve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">2.30.2</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSolve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">2.30.2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">constrains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≤</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">≥</span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.6</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">your</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">compat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">restricts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KernelAbstractions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.10.5</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
